    fix(node): refuse a seed record that declares zero files
    
    A well-formed seed record whose `files` collection is empty certified the node:
    scripts/node_seed_drift.py took node_seed.py check's `PASS ... 0 files present and
    matching` row (exit 0) as a measurement, so a node whose seed applied NOTHING — an
    empty manifest, an empty tar, or a record written before any file was staged —
    reached `RESULT: PASS` and, through scripts/verify-node.sh, `VERIFY: PASS` exit 0.
    CF-291 closed the 0-byte/unparseable record; this is the parseable empty-collection
    case, which stayed green by construction.
    
    Ruling recorded (in the checker's docstring and at finding_empty()): a record that
    declares no files is never a pass, with or without a reason field on it. The record
    was READ and it is conclusively empty, so the verdict is a named FAIL (EXIT_DRIFT,
    exit 1) — not a WARN and not "could not measure". A node that is meant to carry no
    seed should carry no seed record; the absent-record WARN (exit 3) already says that
    honestly, and inventing an opt-out field would let a silent empty collection back in.
    
    What changed:
    - scripts/node_seed_drift.py: `declared_files(doc)` reads the RECORD, not the
      seeder's row, and both modes refuse an empty (or absent / non-list) collection
      BEFORE node_seed.py check runs — the local probe, and the node-side preflight
      (RECORD=3 plus an `EMPTY=empty|absent` token, so the sentence the row prints is
      owned in one place and cannot be copied onto the remote side). `finding_ok()`
      refuses count < 1 as belt and braces, and the PASS row now reads `1 seeded file`
      rather than `1 seeded files`. Exit-code vocabulary and the --json shape unchanged.
    - scripts/verify-node.sh: no new verb and no new branch — the checker's exit 1 is
      already the `bad` case, so the gate answers `VERIFY: FAIL (1)`. The step-6 comment
      now records that, instead of the reader having to infer it.
    - tests/selftest.sh §48 (inside the existing section, no new section): two arms over
      the REAL verifier plus their control.
    - specs/NODE.md and docs/OPERATIONS.md: `N seeded files present and matching` is
      documented as a pass for N > 0 only, and an empty record as a FAIL (CF-379).
    
    Measured before/after, fixture `{"files": []}` at home/.hermes/seed-applied.json:
      before (checker at 226bae2): `  PASS  seed_drift — ...: 0 seeded files present and
        matching` / `RESULT: PASS` / rc=0
      after: `  FAIL  seed_drift — ...: the record declares no files (the files
        collection is empty) — an empty seed certifies nothing` /
        `RESULT: FAIL (the record at ... declares no files)` / rc=1
      same fixture through scripts/verify-node.sh: before `VERIFY: PASS` rc=0, after
        `VERIFY: FAIL (1)` rc=1 (`--strict-seed` also FAIL, rc=1)
      green control (two seeded files): `VERIFY: PASS` rc=0, row `2 seeded files present
        and matching`
      0-byte / corrupt / absent / --strict-seed arms keep their verdicts (WARN exit 3,
        WARN exit 3, WARN exit 3, FAIL exit 1) — re-measured, not assumed.
    
    Discrimination arm, committed rather than ad hoc: the same empty record run through
    the checker at 226bae2 — the row's premise commit, spliced with `git show` so it is
    the real pre-fix file and not a stub of the fix — inside the same verifier prints
    `PASS ... 0 seeded files present and matching` / `VERIFY: PASS` exit 0. The new arm's
    exact condition evaluated ARM=GREEN on this tree and ARM=RED on that tree.
    
    Out of scope, named here: docs/handbook/chapters, docs/handbook/_panel and
    docs/handbook/appendices/units/{31,32,36}-*.md still present `0 seeded files present
    and matching` as a pass and cite node_seed_drift.py line numbers this change shifts —
    those paths belong to the separate panel loop, so they were left untouched and still
    need the same correction. Pre-existing docs/OPERATIONS.md text also still describes
    the pre-CF-063 `${BUNKER_SERVER:?}` guard; that claim was left alone because it is
    another row's business, and nothing here restates it as true.
    
    Guard: `bash tests/selftest.sh` printed `SELFTEST: PASS` at this tree (423 PASS rows,
    61 intentional FAIL rows inside negative fixtures, `359/359 rows parse`);
    `bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh` printed `RESULT: OK` with
    `arms_plan=61 arms_tree=61` (the arms live inside §48, so no census change). The repo
    ships no CI workflow, so no CI run exists for this commit.
    
